# Publish & repo setup — fieldops-ui

Align the installable package with [react-native-builder-bob](https://oss.callstack.com/react-native-builder-bob/build) and requirements. No component implementation rules here — only ship shape.

## Scaffold

- Prefer `create-react-native-library` / bob init for the library root.
- Modern version floor: NativeWind v4 + RN/Expo band that NW v4 documents (design: floor A).
- Support **npm, yarn, and pnpm** equally for consumers and docs. Do not require pnpm-only workspace features for hosts.
- Repo may use one lockfile for development; README install snippets show all three clients.

## Bob build

- `prepare`: `bob build` (works across npm / yarn / pnpm publish and git installs per bob docs).
- Targets: `module` (esm) + `typescript` at minimum. Add `commonjs` only if a real consumer needs it.
- Entry: `main`, `types`, `exports` for `.` and `./preset`.
- Output in `lib/`; gitignore `lib/`.

## Lean npm tarball (industry)

`package.json` `files` whitelist only what hosts need, for example:

- `lib/`
- preset entry file(s) if not already under `lib/`
- `README.md`, `LICENSE`

**Never publish:**

- `example-expo/`, `example-bare/` (or `example/`)
- `__tests__`, fixtures, mocks
- `.cursor/`, agent transcripts, `docs/superpowers/`
- Pods, `node_modules`, build caches

Consumers must not need the source tree when using the published package (requirements). Prefer shipping compiled `lib/` + types; keep className strings intact inside `lib` for NativeWind hosts.

## Dual examples (dev only)

- `example-expo/` — Expo host proving NativeWind wiring + preset.
- `example-bare/` — framework-less RN host proving the same contracts.
- Both consume the library like an external package (workspace/link), not by deep-importing `src/`.
- Both stay out of the npm tarball via `files` (and `.npmignore` if needed).

## Peers

- `react`, `react-native`, `nativewind` as peers (ranges match modern floor).
- Host installs Tailwind / babel / metro pieces per NativeWind docs — do not bundle them into `lib`.

## Security / “obfuscation”

- Open, readable bob output + `.d.ts` — no javascript-obfuscator (breaks Metro / class strings).
- Supply-chain hygiene: no secrets in tarball; lockfile in repo; explicit `exports` so internals stay private.

## Gitignore (minimum)

- `lib/`
- `docs/superpowers/`
- example native build artifacts (`Pods/`, `build/`, `.expo/`)
- `node_modules/`, coverage, OS junk

## Before handoff

`pnpm` / `npm` / `yarn` equivalent of: install → test → lint → build must pass once scripts exist.
